{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 27]], "date-time": "2026-02-27T01:31:45Z", "timestamp": 1772155905747, "version": "3.50.1"}, "reference-count": 70, "publisher": "Scientific Societies", "issue": "8", "funder": [{"DOI": "10.13039/501100012166", "name": "National Key R&D Program of China", "doi-asserted-by": "crossref", "award": ["2021YFD1200600"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["2021YFD1200600"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100012166", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "crossref"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/501100012166", "name": "National Key R&D Program of China", "doi-asserted-by": "crossref", "award": ["2021YFD1401000"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["2021YFD1401000"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100012166", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "crossref"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/501100001809", "name": "National Natural Science Foundation of China", "doi-asserted-by": "crossref", "award": ["32372562"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["32372562"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100001809", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "crossref"}]}, {"name": "Key R&D Program of Qinghai Province in China", "award": ["2022-NK-125"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["2022-NK-125"]}]}, {"name": "Key R&D Program of Yangling Seed Industry Innovation Center", "award": ["Ylzy-xm-01"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["Ylzy-xm-01"]}]}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["Plant Disease"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2024, 8, 1]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>\n                    Fusarium head blight (FHB) is a devastating disease that occurs in warm and humid environments. The German wheat \u2018Centrum\u2019 has displayed moderate to high levels of FHB resistance in the field for many years. In this study, an F\n                    <jats:sub>6:8</jats:sub>\n                    recombinant inbred line (RIL) population derived from cross \u2018Centrum\u2019 \u00d7 \u2018Xinong 979\u2019 was evaluated for FHB response following point inoculation in five environments. The population and parents were genotyped using the GenoBaits Wheat 16 K Panel. Stable quantitative trait loci (QTL) associated with FHB resistance in \u2018Centrum\u2019 were mapped on chromosome arms 2DS and 5BS. The most effective QTL, located in 2DS, was identified as a new chromosome region represented by a 1.4 Mb interval containing 17 candidate genes. Another novel QTL was mapped in chromosome arm 5BS of a 5BS to 7BS translocation chromosome. In addition, two environmentally sensitive QTL were mapped on chromosome arms 2BL from \u2018Centrum\u2019 and 5AS from \u2018Xinong 979\u2019. Polymorphisms of flanking phenotypic variance explained (PVE) markers (allele-specific quantitative PCR [AQP]) AQP-6 for QFhb.nwafu-2DS and 16K-13073 for QFhb.nwafu-5BS were validated in a panel of 217 cultivars and breeding lines. These markers could be useful for marker-assisted selection (MAS) of FHB resistance and provide a starting point for fine mapping and marker-based cloning of the resistance genes.\n                  </jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1094/pdis-01-24-0135-re", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2024, 3, 27]], "date-time": "2024-03-27T15:44:47Z", "timestamp": 1711554287000}, "page": "2462-2471", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 1, "title": ["Identification of Two Novel QTL for Fusarium Head Blight Resistance in German Wheat Cultivar Centrum"], "prefix": "10.1094", "volume": "108", "author": [{"given": "Hui", "family": "Ren", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "State Key Laboratory of Crop Stress Biology for Arid Areas, College of Agronomy, Northwest A&F University, Yangling, Shaanxi 712100, P.R. China"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Xin", "family": "Zhang", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "State Key Laboratory of Crop Stress Biology for Arid Areas, College of Agronomy, Northwest A&F University, Yangling, Shaanxi 712100, P.R. Ch